  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DETERMINING IMPACT OF FISHERIES BYCATCH AND DIRECT TAKE ON THE DEPLETED POPULATION OF LOGGERHEAD TURTLES FROM OMAN (AND OTHER SPECIES) IN THE PERSIAN GULF AND THE GULF OF OMAN - PHASE I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to determine the impact of fisheries bycatch in the Gulf of Oman and the Persian Gulf on the Oman loggerhead nesting population and other sea turtle species in the region. Activities include: 1. a questionnaire will be translated into Farsi; 2 a training workshop will be held for interviewers; 3. teams of 2-4 interviewers will be dispatched at over 20 key fishing sites and ports to interview fishers over 4-6 months; 4. data will be analyzed to determine hotspots of fisher/turtle interaction zones; and 5. results will be presented to key government agencies in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
